{"from": "claim:ac-26-13-14-light-voice", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-09-03-06-road-vision", "note": "Third telling of the conversion: Acts 26 adds noon, a light 'brighter than the sun', the Hebrew language, all companions fallen, and the goads proverb, which 9:3-6 lacks; the core (light from the sky, falling, voice of Jesus) is the same fact."}
{"from": "claim:ac-26-13-14-light-voice", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-22-09-companions-light", "note": "Acts 22:9 says the companions saw the light and did not understand the voice; Acts 26:13-14 has the light around all and 'we had all fallen to the earth' - the retellings differ on the companions."}
{"from": "claim:ac-26-14-goads-proverb", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-09-03-06-road-vision", "note": "The goads saying appears only in the Acts 26 retelling; Acts 9:4 (and 22:7) lack it - the fetched Wikipedia 'Acts 26' article states this explicitly."}
{"from": "claim:ac-26-15-18-commission", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-09-03-06-road-vision", "note": "The 26 retelling adds the commission content (servant and witness; open their eyes; darkness to light; Satan to God) not in the Acts 9 telling."}
{"from": "claim:ac-26-19-20-obedience-preaching", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-09-19-22-preached-damascus", "note": "Same Damascus preaching; Acts 26:20 adds Jerusalem, all Judea and the Gentiles, and repentance language."}
{"from": "claim:ac-26-09-11-persecution-vote", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-22-04-persecution", "note": "The same persecution report; Acts 26 adds the authority from the chief priests, the vote against those put to death, and the synagogues."}
{"from": "claim:ac-26-05-pharisee-strictest", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-22-03-gamaliel-jerusalem", "note": "Both are Paul's self-reports of Pharisaic exactness; 22:3 has training under Gamaliel in the strict tradition, 26:5 names the sect as 'the strictest' (akribeistaten)."}
{"from": "claim:ac-26-28-christian-name", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-11-26-christian-name", "note": "Acts 11:26 records the name's origin in Antioch; Acts 26:28 shows Agrippa using the name c. 59/60 - the name's currency, not its origin, is the claim here."}
{"from": "claim:ac-26-32-appeal-prevented-release", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-25-10-11-appeal-caesar", "note": "The consequence of the appeal: Agrippa says Paul might have been freed had he not appealed."}
{"from": "claim:ac-26-30-31-withdrew-agreed", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-25-25-nothing-worthy-death", "note": "Agrippa's circle reach the same judgment as Festus: nothing worthy of death or bonds."}
{"from": "claim:ac-26-21-seized-temple", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-21-30-city-uproar", "note": "Same event told later: the temple seizure and the attempt to kill Paul (Acts 21:30-31)."}
